# Demon Wall: "Defender" and "As long as this creature has a counter on it, it can attack as though it didn't have defender"
# (CR 702.3b, 609.4), and "{5}{B}: Put two +1/+1 counters on this creature." Turn 3, the Wall has been under Bot1's control
# since turn 1 and has no counter: defender stops it attacking (the refusal) while the Ornithopter beside it attacks (the
# control; a 0/2, it deals nothing). In the second main phase Bot1 pays {5}{B} and the Wall gets two +1/+1 counters. Turn 5 it
# attacks on its own as a 5/5 and becomes tapped (CR 508.1f: it has no vigilance), Bot2 going from 20 to 15. It still
# has defender while it attacks: "as though" changes only whether it may attack (CR 609.4), so its keywords are Defender and
# Menace.

